    shadow: 'Taken too far, formlessness becomes emptiness: people struggle to trust someone who stands for nothing, and allies tire of a partner who changes every season. Constant reinvention can mean never building anything that lasts, since institutions, friendships and crafts all need some fixed shape to grow around. Some commitments, such as loyalty and principle, are strong precisely because they don’t bend. The wiser player is fluid in method and solid in values.',
